[{"id":"enc-fill-onehot","itemId":"state-encoding","role":"warmup","promptHtml":"Lesson 5.3's one-hot door gives each state a bit of its own: <code class=\"nobreak\">CLOSED</code> is <code class=\"nobreak\">3'b001</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">OPEN</code> is <code class=\"nobreak\">3'b010</code>. Type <code class=\"nobreak\">LOCKED</code>'s code.","explanationHtml":"<p>One-hot means exactly one bit is 1, and each state has a different one. <code class=\"nobreak\">CLOSED</code> has bit 0 and <code class=\"nobreak\">OPEN</code> bit 1, so <code class=\"nobreak\">LOCKED</code> gets bit 2: <code class=\"nobreak\">3'b100</code>. It is the bit <code class=\"nobreak\">is_locked</code> reads.</p>","type":"fill","file":"hdl/level-05/door_onehot/door_onehot.sv","firstLine":12,"totalLines":37,"before":["  typedef enum logic [2:0] {","    CLOSED = 3'b001,","    OPEN   = 3'b010,"],"blankLine":{"left":"    LOCKED = ","right":""},"after":["  } state_t;"],"highlighted":{"before":[[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"typedef","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"enum","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" [","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"2","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"{","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false}],[{"text":"    CLOSED ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"3'b001","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":",",